{"id": "879c0f75-f7e5-460a-9eb1-e3614cdcebf1", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review the auroradataapi cluster in us-east-1. I'm checking Multi-AZ and reader placement, backup retention, deletion protection, and engine version currency. I'm not looking at anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_jLe9q9387ahs80ojpZYalt", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "aurora-reliability-review", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only RDS reliability review of ONE Aurora cluster: auroradataapi ([redacted ARN]), account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1.",
  "scope_restrictions": "Do NOT list, describe, or scan any other clusters, instances, or regions. Only describe this cluster and the member instances that belong to it (as listed in its DBClusterMembers). Read-only calls only; make no changes.",
  "checks": [
    "1. Multi-AZ and reader placement: cluster MultiAZ flag, AvailabilityZones, each member instance (identifier, role writer/reader, AZ, instance class, PromotionTier, status). Flag if there are no readers, all instances are in one AZ, or the writer has no failover target in a different AZ. Note if it is Aurora Serverless v2 or provisioned.",
    "2. Backup retention and deletion protection: BackupRetentionPeriod, PreferredBackupWindow, DeletionProtection, copy-tags-to-snapshot, and whether automated backups/latest restorable time look healthy. Flag retention below 7 days as a concern (note 1 day is the minimum/weak) and deletion protection disabled.",
    "3. Engine version currency: Engine, EngineVersion, and AutoMinorVersionUpgrade on members. Compare against the latest available minor version for the same major version and against the newest supported major version (use describe-db-engine-versions filtered to that engine, scoped to this engine only; this is a global engine catalog lookup and not a scan of other clusters). Note whether the version is nearing or past end of standard support if determinable (verify via AWS docs with verify_aws_claim if needed), and any pending maintenance actions for this cluster only."
  ],
  "output": "Return concise findings: for each of the 3 areas give current values, status (OK / Warning / Risk), and a specific recommended remediation. Include a short overall summary. State clearly any item you couldn't determine and why (e.g. access denied)."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review Aurora cluster auroradataapi reliability settings in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

